You mean, you fear that? But even if there *is* one with a wand of
death, as long as you stand not in line-of-sight and play the Game
of Drawbridge Guillotine you have nothing to fear. Once the court
yard is cleared you may enter the castle to get the wand and wish
for reflection and/or magic resistance. (Take care of the eels in
the moat, though, or _burn_ Elbereth on the square where you play
the game of GDG.)

> Anything I didn't think of?  Or other wisdom?

Other possibilities...
Have you found Fort Ludios? There are some dragons there and maybe
they leave silver or gray scales.
In your set of unidentified rings there's no levitation I guess?
Have you access to the fountains in the upper levels to uncurse
your boots of levitation? If successful enter the castle from the
back door; let the soldiers (if any) drop through the trapdoors
and get the wand of wishing when the central court is clear. Or
see whether one of the four dragons leaves grey or silver scales.

But the most simple is Castle Guillotine. And a wand of sleeping
would be helpful (as is the wand of teleportation), just in case.

Your quest artifact allows you to levelport beyond the castle; you
may either proceed with the Valley or use it to get to the castles
back door. There you can (if you still have one) read a scroll of
earth to cover some (never all!) of the trapdoors to reach the
dragon chambers (scales!?) even if you lack levitation or jumping.

